--- !u!114 &5551166701328841805
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1961217864587457082}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 39494524dd17c314297476e7d6ff65a8, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogueLines:
  - "He wasn\u2019t trying to be a hero, he just wanted to help. The boring kind
    of good. Showing up. Stepping in. Making things quieter, not louder. He didn\u2019t
    even like the uniform all that much. \u2018It makes conversations shorter.\u2019 
    People stopped talking like humans once they saw it. He said it mattered to be
    seen doing the right thing. Maybe it would make the jokes stop."
  - "That night he was off duty. No uniform. No badge out. He saw the cars and ran
    anyway; because someone needed help and he was right there. That\u2019s it. I
    keep thinking about that part. How instinct still overrode fear.\r\n"
  - "Now everyone wants to argue about procedures, about what should have happened.
    About how fast decisions are made. No one wants to talk about how hard he worked
    to be seen as trustworthy. How careful he was. How often he swallowed things
    just to keep the peace. \u2018It was a mistake.\u2019 - My ass. That word feels
    too clean. Like something you wipe up and forget."
  - "He learned this place\u2019s rules better than most people born into them. And
    still, it wasn\u2019t enough. I keep finding myself defending him to strangers.
    As if love needs documentation. He deserved to be met as a person first. That\u2019s
    the part they skipped.\u201D"
  dialogueText: {fileID: 0}
  typingSpeed: 0.05
  delayBetweenLines: 1
